From b1517fd8ebcbb54909fa2130108a0339012d67cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:21:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Name every registered action and handle duplicates explicitly
 (issue 8)

registerActions used a default id of "<screen>:action", so a second call on
the same screen silently piled up parallel edges. Re-registering an existing
screen id was ignored without a word.

- registerActions(screen, { name: { actions, to?, cost?, name?, meta? } }).
  The name is the node id. Unnamed input is rejected with a message that
  shows the right call. Nodes record meta.parent.
- onDuplicate: "error" (default) | "skip" | "replace" for screens and
  explicit edge ids. Replace only touches dynamic items, rebuilds the edges
  of a replaced screen with stable ids, and keeps the old item when the
  replacement fails validation.
- Tests and docs updated.

